{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The golden fixture for the steward key, the commit MAC, the sealed stamp, the head log copy, the veto frame and the repair notice (mls/core/src/steward.rs; not part of this specification).",
    "All integers big-endian. HKDF is HKDF-SHA256 with an empty salt; AEAD is AES-256-GCM with a 12-byte nonce; signatures are Ed25519.",
    "Frames nest: envelope (kind 2) -> optional veto frame ff 56 54 01 || BE16(169) || signed veto || inner -> optional carried frame ff 4c 43 01 ... -> raw commit. signed veto = 01 || handle || BE64(E) || vetoed next || replacement next || signature.",
    "Every build reads all of it and writes none of it (constants.stewardWrites is false).",
    "Written by an independent implementation (Node crypto), so the Rust replay is a second opinion. Replayed through the fixture door (kind \"steward\") in Rust, JavaScript and Swift (and, in Peachy's Android client, Kotlin)."
  ],
